cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "healpix-resample: PSF-aware resampling tools for HEALPix Earth-observation grids"
abstract: >-
  A lightweight, GPU-friendly Python package for regridding data from
  unstructured longitude/latitude samples onto a HEALPix grid. Every resampler
  builds a sparse PyTorch operator mapping input samples to a subset of HEALPix
  cells at a chosen resolution level. The PSFResampler treats projected-grid
  pixels as sparse, spatially weighted measurements of an unknown HEALPix field
  and recovers that field through a matrix-free weighted least-squares problem,
  jointly accounting for the sensor point spread function and the
  source-to-HEALPix geometry.
